  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "beat-1",
      "index": 0,
      "assets": {},
      "duration": 37.134,
      "audio": {
        "id": "subtitle-clock-beat-1"
      },
      "narration": "The blue sine curve peaks at one, bottoms at minus one, and repeats after two pi. Now watch the teal copy as we double the input. Follow its peak and next zero as they move; compare their horizontal positions with the blue landmarks. Both end halfway toward the vertical axis! Twice the new x gives the old input, so the output stays the same. Sine of twice x compresses horizontally, not vertically. The amplitude remains one, but a full cycle now spans pi: half the period.",
      "visualDescription": "Content needed: One continuous shared graph on a black field, with x in radians from 0 to 2π and y covering −1 to 1 with margin. Keep the blue reference y = sin(x) visible throughout. Introduce a teal coincident copy, then continuously change it from sin(x) to sin(2x). Track its first peak and following zero against fixed blue landmarks: π/2 → π/4 and π → π/2, with heights unchanged. Let viewers inspect these correspondences during the second narration block; withhold halfway labels until Reveal. Show the unchanged amplitude using the same y = ±1 reference heights, then compare cycle spans 2π and π. No title card, decorative motion, or extra scene.\nNotes: Subtitles are the narration track. Approximately 92 spoken words; target 40–43 seconds at a readable pace, subject to measured subtitle alignment. No explicit silence. Use 2D, main orbit false, interactions empty. Retain the main curves and graph through the ending.\n",
